      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Ruth Halloran managed the grocery through the ration months: one basket a household, cash or relief scrip, and the walk-in tagged by the Cordon for a relief drive that never came to collect. Northline's reefer was turned back at the roadblock and its driver parked it behind the store and walked. Aisle three came down on a fight over the last of the bleach and nobody stood it back up. When Danny, the stock boy, was bitten on the dock he asked to sit in the cold room where it was cool, and Ruth locked him in and wired a battery alarm from the hardware store to the door so she would hear him if he tried it. Sal never left his counter. Ruth climbed to her office on the mezzanine with the walk-in key, sat down in her chair to listen, and is sitting there still.",
